Z||000011||Fformula88||11-06-2001||10:33 AM||||I agree that these Mustang bashing threads are getting old.  Really old.  The real reason is why do Fiero owners find it necessary to pick on Mustangs?  Lets investigate.<P>1. Some don't like them because lots of people own them.  These owner prefer cars that are more unique so they stand out more.  I also like cars that are unique on the road, which may be the biggest reason I like Fiero's.  They are unique in nearly every respect.  But this doesn't make the Mustang bad.  Maybe the 170,000 new 'Stang buyers a year know something we don't?<P>2. Some people don't like Mustangs becasue they offer less than perfect handling.  They are a bit heavy to be tossed around in the manner a Fiero can.  Its the price one pays for big horsepower and torque I guess.  However, to say they handle bad is just showing ones lack of knowledge about them.<P>3. Some are just Chevy/Pontiac fans and hate Ford because its not the General.  I am not getting into this loosing battle to convince them otherwise.<P>They are not pure sports cars (like a 'Vette or Porsche) but they fulfill their mission in life rather well.  They offer a lot of drivetrain in a RWD package for a cheap price in a package that has got to have such an advantage on the F-body twins that its wiped them out of the market.<P>Mustangs are plentiful, and they will continue to be so for a long time.  Better get used to seeing lots of them. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||stsmithgt||11-06-2001||11:14 AM||||I'd like to try out that new Mustang coming out with independant rear susupension.  It's about time they started introducing that to their cars.||||reg||1
Z||000013||turbo86se||11-06-2001||11:52 AM||||I see lots and lots of Camaros down here, recently saw a new Vette destroy a new Camaro, that was funny!<BR>Personally, Mustangs and Camaros don't do anything for me, I like the cars, but I'd never own one. A friend of mine drives a Mustang Cobra, '99 I think, it's a blast to drive, another friend drives a '00 Camaro SS. It's pretty quick too. Cool thing is, those two guys are dying to go for a ride in my turbo-charged V6 Fiero, and are in awe of everything you can do to a Fiero.<BR>On the other hand, another friend, who drives a '99 Eclipse turbo, always gives me sh!& about Fieros being junk and all, until I showed him my SE up close, he had no idea the engine was in the back! Idiot! He has no credibility when it comes to Fieros. <P>I think I got a little too off topic, then again, so is the post!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by turbo86se (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
